# Add pen material texture paper effects and decorative themes

## Scope and existing evidence

Render aesthetic headings with adjustable marker lettering, highlighter
strokes, ink color and thickness. Preserve legible body text and allow paper
textures or shadows to be disabled for preprinted notebook sheets.

This is unfinished implementation work. The following original design
records remain accepted theoretical deliverables and are not reopened:

- ATR-P5-002 — archived render design
- ATR-P5-003 — archived render design
- ATR-P5-006 — archived render design
- ATR-P5-007 — archived render design

## Native heading lettering pigment and weight (partial) — 2026-11-03

The existing Rust `atrament-profiles notebook --flow-markdown` compiler now
accepts opt-in `--heading-ink-color '#RRGGBB'` and
`--heading-ink-scale 100..250`. These style the **authored glyph ink** in
`#`/`##`/`###` heading rows, independently of the ordinary underline,
double underline or `--heading-style marker` backdrop color.

The original
canonical glyph TSV, geometry, seeded per-occurrence variation and all
non-heading content remain unchanged. Stroke thickness is multiplied after
optional mean-profile scaling; a physical pen width above 1500 µm or
outside page margins refuses before replacing an existing output. This
only multiplies pen width, not glyph height or ideal curve geometry.

Two native regressions check all three heading levels beside paragraph and
list body rows, exact page-specific physical ink segments and RGB, unchanged
source glyphs, genuine deterministic PDF/transparent PNG output, and atomic
rejection of duplicate, malformed, outside-range or oversized controls.
The feature has no independently persisted style settings or browser-driven
native rendering. It does not yet provide marker-shaped glyph lettering,
opacity/translucent material, calibrated texture or continuous cursive, so
P5-014 remains open.

## Bounded native marker-band pen weight (partial) — 2026-11-04

`atrament-profiles notebook --flow-markdown` accepts
`--heading-style marker --heading-marker-scale 50..105` to alter the
**underlay** pen width for the #/##/### marker hierarchy without touching
caller-authored lettering, plain body ink, or the underlying stroke TSV.

The previous default remains exactly 100%. The upper bound reflects the
native 1500-µm maximum pen width: a primary 1400-µm marker cannot safely
be enlarged further, and invalid, repeated or non-marker options refuse
rather than silently clamping. PDF and transparent PNG reflect the same
selected physical strokes. The new native subprocess regression checks
three heading tiers at 50%, 100% and 105% alongside ordinary body ink,
and verifies that rejected options preserve the existing PDF bytes.

This changes opaque stroke widths, **not** translucent ink material,
highlighter opacity, digital-only shadows, or the shape of the glyphs.
The broader P5-014 acceptance remains open.

## Acceptance decision

Open. The finite implementation described above is not established by
the original theoretical design acceptance. This follow-up must be
evaluated separately against its practical or theoretical scope.
